diff --git a/NOTES.md b/NOTES.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..c5780b4
--- /dev/null
+++ b/NOTES.md
@@ -0,0 +1,101 @@
+# Credit control – implementation notes
+
+Nothing could be run here (no shell, no database), so none of this has been executed. It was written against the
+existing code and checked by reading only. First thing to do on a test copy: run update 44, then walk through the
+flows below.
+
+## Key design decision: credit status reuses what webERP already has
+
+webERP already has a customer "credit status" (`debtorsmaster.holdreason` -> `holdreasons.dissallowinvoices`:
+0 normal, 1 no invoicing, 2 "watch" warning). Order entry (`SelectOrderItems`), counter sales, special orders,
+contracts, receipts and the inquiry pages already test it, and the live system's existing stop list is
+presumably already expressed that way. So:
+
+* **Stop** = customer moved to the hold reason in config `CreditStopReason` (code 92, `dissallowinvoices=1`).
+* **Watch** = `CreditWatchReason` (code 91, `dissallowinvoices=2`). **Release** = `CreditNormalReason`.
+* No new status column, so there is one source of truth and the existing pages keep working. BR-40: customers already
+  on a hold reason that blocks invoicing are on stop from day one with no data load.
+* `CreditStatus.php` (hold reason maintenance) could previously only save 0/1, which would have silently turned
+  a watch code into "normal" and a stop code into "normal" on edit. It now offers Normal / Watch / Stop, and it
+  refuses to change the setting of, or delete, the three codes credit control uses.
+* `SelectOrderItems.php`: the branch used when a customer places their own order blocked every non-zero status,
+  i.e. also watch. Fixed to block only stop and warn on watch (BR-08, BR-11).
+
+## What was built
+
+**Schema** (`sql/updates/44.php`, and the same in `install/sql/tables/*.sql` + `install/sql/data/*.sql`, because a
+fresh install never runs the numbered updates):
+* tables `creditreviews`, `creditlog` (insert-only audit trail of every credit control action), `dunninglevels`,
+  `dunninglog`, `creditcharges` (unique per customer + month = no double charging), `creditwriteoffs`.
+* `debtorsmaster`: `nextreviewdate`, `exemptinterest`, `exemptfees`, `dunninghold`; `debtortrans.disputed`.
+* system types 80 interest, 81 late fee, 82 waiver, 83 write-off, so each shows as its own item on statements and
+  inquiries.
+* config values (review period, interest rate, late fee, days before charging, GL accounts, approval limit, minimum
+  days between letters, the three hold reason codes), hold reasons 91/92 (and a normal one if the site has none),
+  3 default letter stages, security token 21, scripts, menu items.
+* The update is idempotent, records itself only when `Errors == 0` (the #304 rule, which most recent files dropped),
+  gives every existing customer a next review date and a default for the hold reasons. Demo databases are at update
+  17 so they run it on first login.
+
+**Pages** (all new, in the project's style: `DB_query`, `__()`, `prnMsg`, FormID):
+* `CreditReview.php` – per customer: status, limit, balance, overdue, last reminder stage, next review; record a
+  review (limit change happens in the same transaction), change status with reason, exemptions, mark invoices
+  disputed, add a note (for agency/legal action outside the system); review history and the full credit history.
+* `CreditControlReport.php` – due/overdue reviews, over limit (and by how much), watch/stop, open orders of watched
+  customers; filter by rep and currency; home-currency totals; plus the ledger-vs-customer-accounts comparison by
+  transaction type (BR-37/38).
+* `DunningRun.php` – preview, untick customers, send. Letters are emailed (`SendEmailFromWebERP`), no-email customers
+  are listed for posting. Stage is recomputed at send time from what is still overdue.
+* `CreditCharges.php` – month-end preview/confirm/post of interest and fees, and waiver with reason.
+* `CreditWriteOff.php` – write-off, approval queue, period report.
+* `CreditControlSetup.php` – Finance's settings and letter stages/wording.
+* `CustomerCredit.php` – portal page (reminders, interest/fees, balance).
+* `includes/CreditControlFunctions.php` – shared helpers (status, history log, posting a charge/credit to the
+  customer account and GL, allocation, overdue query, rep restriction).
+
+**Enforcement of stop on every route** (BR-06): `DeliveryDetails.php` (order commit – covers a customer stopped after
+the order was started), `ConfirmDispatch_Invoice.php` (dispatch/invoice of existing orders), `EDIProcessOrders.php`,
+`RecurringSalesOrdersProcess.php` (template is left untouched so it is raised after release), `api_salesorders.php`
+(order creation and `InvoiceSalesOrder` – this is the web shop's route; new error code `CustomerOnStop` 1158).
+Counter sales, special orders and `SelectOrderItems` were already blocked by the existing mechanism.
+
+**Other existing code changed:** `Customers.php` (new customers get a next review date; limit/status changes made on
+the customer page are written to the credit history; customers with credit history cannot be deleted – the history
+cannot be deleted and the new tables have foreign keys), `Z_ChangeCustomerCode.php` (copies the new customer columns,
+repoints the new tables), `SelectCustomer.php` (menu link), staff guide `doc/Manual/ManualAccountsReceivable.html`
+(new Credit Control section incl. the sales note), `doc/NEWS.md`.
+
+## Decisions on the BRD's open questions
+
+1. Interest: simple annual rate / 12 per month on overdue invoices, one rate for all currencies. 2. Late fee: one flat fee
+per customer per month, set in home currency and converted. 3. No interest on interest/fees (only invoices, type 10, are
+chased or charged). 4. No automatic stop after the final letter: the run flags final-notice customers for Maria.
+5. Over-limit orders: see "not done". 6. Approval limit is a setting (default 1000, home currency); the Finance Director
+approves, no accountant sign-off. 7. A payment received later against a written-off debt arrives as a normal
+unallocated receipt – it is not specially marked. 8. Reps see the status and hold reason. 9. Letters are one language,
+editable by Finance. 10. Watch is not shown in the portal. 11. Cover when both are away: anyone with security token 3
+(and token 21 for approvals) – managed through the normal role setup. 12. Limits are per customer account (`debtorno`),
+as webERP already models it; branches do not have their own.
+
+Other choices: security uses existing token 3 ("Credit notes and AR management", already guarding `Customers.php` and
+credit notes) for credit control and a new token 21 for write-off approval, granted to role 8 – give 21 to the FD's role.
+Pages open to reps (token 2) restrict to their own customers (`SalesmanLogin`) and only act for token 3. The portal
+page identifies the customer from `www_users`, never from the request (`$_SESSION['CustomerID']` is overwritten by staff
+pages, so it is not safe). Letters already sent before a customer's last payment (`lastpaiddate`) do not count towards
+"already sent", so a customer who pays and later falls behind again starts at the right stage. Write-offs are posted at
+the rate the written-off items were booked at (weighted), allocated oldest first, so debtors control falls by exactly what
+those items added: no exchange difference to post and the ledger stays in step. Waivers reverse only the unpaid part of a charge.
+
+## Not done / known gaps
+
+* **Over-limit orders held for approval (BR-10)**: not built. webERP only has the existing `CheckCreditLimits` setting
+  (warn / prohibit). Holding orders needs an order hold flag and release step through dispatch; I'd treat it as its own
+  change. Use "Prohibit" for now; over-limit customers are on the credit control report.
+* **Aged debtors report (BR-31)** does not yet show credit status/limit/last stage (it is a multi-query PDF/CSV report);
+  those are on the credit control report and the review page instead.
+* The web shop's own pages are not in this repository; it is protected through the API errors above.
+* Portal page has no menu entry for customer roles; link it from their menu as needed.
+* Legacy `sql/mysql/*.sql` upgrade scripts and `sql/demo.sql` / `install/sql/demo.sql` were not touched
+  (the numbered update handles them).
+* Not run: PHP syntax, the SQL, and the flows need testing. Locale `.pot` not regenerated.
+* Post-go-live data load of the spreadsheet stop list/limits is done through the existing customer or CSV import pages.
