+							INNER JOIN holdreasons ON debtorsmaster.holdreason = holdreasons.reasoncode
+							WHERE debtorsmaster.debtorno = '" . $OrderHeader['debtorno'] . "'");
+	$StopRow = DB_fetch_row($StopResult);
+	if (DB_num_rows($StopResult) > 0 and $StopRow[0] == 1) {
+		$Errors[] = CustomerOnStop;
+		return $Errors;
+	}
+
 	$TaxProvResult = api_DB_query("SELECT taxprovinceid FROM locations WHERE loccode='" . $OrderHeader['fromstkloc'] ."'");
 	if (DB_error_no() != 0) {
 		$Errors[] = NoTaxProvince;
diff --git a/doc/Manual/ManualAccountsReceivable.html b/doc/Manual/ManualAccountsReceivable.html
index c7bb00d..c1b8b54 100644
--- a/doc/Manual/ManualAccountsReceivable.html
+++ b/doc/Manual/ManualAccountsReceivable.html
@@ -189,6 +189,35 @@
 <p>If the customer has any contacts that have the statement flag set then it will not be possible to print their statement so as to avoid sending both a printed statement and an email statement</p>
 
 
+<div class="floatright">
+    <a class="minitext" href="#top">⬆ Top</a>
+</div>
+
+<h2><a id="CreditControl">Credit Control</a></h2>
+
+<p>Credit control is done by users with the Credit notes and AR management security token (the credit controller and the deputy). Finance sets up credit control on the <em>Credit Control Setup</em> page: the standard review period, the interest rate and late fee, the General Ledger accounts they are posted to, the write-off approval limit and the number, timing and wording of the reminder letters. Sales reps and sales office staff can look at credit information but cannot change it. A sales rep only ever sees his own customers.</p>
+
+<h3><a id="CreditReview">Credit Reviews</a></h3>
+<p>Open <em>Credit status, reviews and credit history</em> from the customer menu. A review records the date, who did it, the outcome (limit confirmed, raised or reduced, put on watch, put on stop, or taken off watch/stop), the new limit, notes and the next review date. If the limit changes the customer's limit is updated by the same action. Reviews cannot be changed or deleted. Every customer has a next review date: new customers get one from the standard review period, and the <em>Credit Control Report</em> lists the customers whose review is due, those over their credit limit (and by how much) and those on watch or on stop, by sales rep and currency, with totals in the home currency.</p>
+
+<h3><a id="CreditStopWatch">Stop and Watch</a></h3>
+<p>The credit status of a customer is the existing Credit Status code on the customer: a code that does not allow invoicing is <b>stop</b>, a code set to <em>Watch</em> is <b>watch</b>. A customer on stop cannot have an order entered in the sales office or the web shop, received by EDI, raised from a standing order, dispatched or invoiced until credit control takes the customer off stop. A customer on watch can still be supplied, but whoever takes the order is shown a warning and credit control can see the open orders of watched customers on the Credit Control Report. Every change of status or limit is recorded with who, when and why in the customer's credit history.</p>
+
+<h3><a id="DunningRun">Overdue Reminder Run</a></h3>
+<p>Run <em>Overdue Reminder Run</em> weekly. It shows each overdue customer, the stage of letter they will get, the invoices and the email address. Untick the customers to leave out (a promise to pay) and send. Letters are emailed to the customer's contact flagged to receive statements; customers without an email address are listed so the letter can be posted. A customer moves up a stage only if they are still overdue, never receives the same stage twice, and does not receive letters less than the minimum number of days apart. Invoices marked <em>disputed</em> on the credit review page are not chased and do not attract interest. A customer can be left out of all runs from the credit review page.</p>
+
+<h3><a id="CreditCharges">Month End Interest and Late Fees</a></h3>
+<p>At month end run <em>Month End Interest and Late Fees</em>. The page lists what each customer will be charged; tick the customers and post. Interest is the annual rate divided by 12 on invoices that are overdue by more than the charging days (interest and fees themselves are never charged interest); the late fee is one flat fee per customer per month. They are posted in the customer's currency as separate items that appear on the statement, and to the General Ledger income accounts. A customer can only be charged once for a month, and customers exempt from interest or fees (set on the credit review page) are skipped. A charge can be waived with a reason from the same page; the waiver is posted to the ledger too.</p>
+
+<h3><a id="CreditWriteOff">Bad Debt Write-offs</a></h3>
+<p>A write-off of all or part of what a customer owes is entered on <em>Bad Debt Write-offs</em> with a reason. Write-offs above the approval limit wait for approval by the Finance Director on the same page and have no effect until approved. A posted write-off reduces the customer balance, is posted to the bad debt account and puts the customer on stop unless the tick box is cleared. The page also reports the write-offs over a period with who requested and who approved them.</p>
+
+<h3><a id="CreditPortal">Customer Portal</a></h3>
+<p>Customers who log in can see the reminders sent to them and the interest and fees charged to their account on <em>My Reminders and Charges</em>. They only ever see their own account, and their watch status is not shown.</p>
+
+<h3><a id="CreditSalesNote">Note for Sales Staff</a></h3>
+<p><b>Watch</b> means the customer can still be supplied but you are warned: speak to credit control before taking a large order. <b>Stop</b> means no order can be taken or released for the customer by any route: contact credit control, who are the only people who can take the customer off stop or change the credit limit. You can see the status, limit, balance, overdue amount and reminders of your own customers on the credit review page.</p>
+
 <div class="floatright">
     <a class="minitext" href="#top">⬆ Top</a>
 </div>
